"digest":"sha256:c3994764440a6669ad2d13fae980114f9dd72bfdef5509c3e3acb51dfb9796ae","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-09-15T02:50:06Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T02:50:06Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/DaviBaum/oma-ananke-backup/releases/download/validated-compact-pressure-2026-09-15/RESTORE-F73-PORTABLE.md"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DaviBaum/oma-ananke-backup/tarball/validated-compact-pressure-2026-09-15","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DaviBaum/oma-ananke-backup/zipball/validated-compact-pressure-2026-09-15","body":"This Windows checkpoint contains the compact branching-tree generator and strengthened pressure verification backend, application source `f73a8793ae0df76d9ec53400cec18b05d2731f63c735b225c2246fee62df6b21`.\n\nThe backend generates two- through eight-terminal alternatives from individual tee sites and connector choices. Its optional compact proof checks exact finite counts and the nominal top-K assignments without materializing the full assignment list. An authored eight-terminal catalogue contains 166,262,214,109,624 connector-ID assignments; this is a finite nominal count, not a count of different physical geometries or an unrestricted physical optimum. Factorized pressure proofs preserve shared coefficient identity and the original physical inputs and flow box. Native geometry, same-model local/global pressure proofs and all-port delivery/velocity checks remain required before acceptance and fresh exported-IFC verification.\n\nValidation binds 114 application files, 305 test/support inputs and 3,275 exact test identities. The original and separately built native environments each passed all 3,275 tests. The bundled runtime passed 3,272; three named virtual-environment bridge tests do not apply to its direct interpreter and passed in both other environments. Generated four-through-eight-terminal analytic fixtures completed native acceptance and fresh export. All three saved Office IFC export roles passed fresh bundled native checks and independent receipt/proof review. These results retain their separate models and scopes.\n\nDownload all three release assets: the ZIP, archive manifest and restore instructions. Verify the ZIP SHA-256 before extracting to a new directory. Read `f73-checkpoint-documentation/CHECKPOINT.md` first, then launch `OMA.cmd` inside the separate sealed package folder. The ZIP accounts for both the immutable package and the separately indexed current documentation companion. The package defaults to port 8765; the existing validated workspace service at port 8768 is a separate instance.\n\nOriginal mathematics, full production readiness and whole-hospital verification remain incomplete. The seven-discipline hospital campaign requires resolved alignment; the separate architecture-only native-clearance run timed out after 1,800 seconds without accepting a candidate. Their original inputs, alternatives, partial IFC, failures and logs are backed up with the repository. The [initial recovery release](https://github.com/DaviBaum/oma-ananke-backup/releases/tag/backup-2026-09-15) contains original mathematical documents, hospital datasets, Store backup and saved UI work; this runtime ZIP does not replace that data backup. Earlier sealed packages remain intact.\n\nSee the [current checkpoint](https://github.com/DaviBaum/oma-ananke-backup/blob/master/docs/PROGRESS.md), [API workflow and examples](https://github.com/DaviBaum/oma-ananke-backup/blob/master/docs/shared-tree-generation.md), and [backup/restore guide](https://github.com/DaviBaum/oma-ananke-backup/blob/master/docs/GITHUB_BACKUP.md).\n"}